{"The helper calls are async, but the loop does not await them before the handler continues and returns success. A failed or slow update to cancelled can leave an email reminder active, and a failed or slow Twilio cancellation can leave an SMS reminder scheduled for a cancelled booking.": 0.9685044288635254, "When a booking is cancelled shortly before a scheduled email reminder, the branch only marks the row as cancelled and waits for the cron to call SendGrid. If the SendGrid send time arrives before the next cron run, the reminder can still be delivered for the cancelled booking.": 0.9674690961837769, "The whole cancellation batch shares one try block, so a single SendGrid error exits the loop before later cancelled reminders are processed. A stale or already-sent batch id can make every following reminder in this cron run stay scheduled and still send.": 0.9914537668228149, "The try block starts async cancellations for the original booking but does not wait for them, so async failures are not caught and the reschedule flow can continue to create the new booking. The old booking's scheduled reminders can remain active alongside the new booking's reminders.": 0.9666317105293274, "When a workflow step is edited, the loop starts cancellation of the reminders from the old step settings but does not wait before continuing to schedule replacements. A slow or failed cancellation can leave the old reminder scheduled, so the booking can receive both the old and new workflow reminder.": 0.9798623919487}